#!/usr/bin/env -S uv run --quiet --script
# /// script
# dependencies = [
#   "duckdb>=0.10.0",
#   "pandas>=2.0.0",
#   "numpy>=1.24.0",
#   "pyarrow>=14.0",
#   "pyyaml>=6.0",
#   "tqdm>=4.66",
# ]
# ///
"""ant-gene-variance-precompute -- fleet-wide gene x facet variability.

Precomputes per-(dataset, gene, facet) between-group variance for the
"hot" gene set already present in ``<h5adstore>/gene_stats_index.parquet``.
Feeds ``/api/databases/{db_id}/gene-variance-by-facet``: the endpoint
hits the aggregate parquet first, only falling back to live DuckDB
compute for datasets not represented here.

Architecture mirrors ``ant-gene-stats-precompute`` and
``ant-module-variability``:

  * Per-dataset parquet cache under
    ``<h5adstore>/_gene_variance_cache/<db_id>/genevar.parquet``.
    Invalidated by mtime comparison against the dataset's ``.duckdb``,
    its by-gene parquet sidecar, and its ``.md`` (facet renames / obs
    derives live there).
  * ``multiprocessing.Pool`` over the dataset queue. Default 2 workers
    (host memory is often under pressure -- the by-gene parquet can be
    5-15 GB per dataset in the DuckDB working set).
  * ``tqdm`` progress + JSON progress lines to stderr every 10
    datasets.
  * Streaming aggregate write via ``duckdb.COPY`` -- never holds >1
    dataset's worth of rows in Python at once.

Output schema (wide, one row per (dataset, gene, facet)):

  ``dataset, gene, facet, facet_type, layer, n_cells, n_groups,
    eta_squared, F_stat, signal, total_var, group_means_json,
    src_fingerprint``.

Where:

  * ``src_fingerprint`` = per-dataset JSON snapshot of the duckdb and
    by-gene parquet (size + mtime); ant-serve skips rows whose sources
    changed after this run. See ``lib/index_freshness.py``.

  * ``signal`` = ``VAR_SAMP(mean_expr_per_group)`` -- kept for backward
    compatibility with the existing endpoint's ranking metric.
  * ``eta_squared`` = SS_between / SS_total on per-cell expression
    values (categorical grouping, matches the module-variability
    formula).
  * ``F_stat`` = one-way F for the same grouping. NaN if any group has
    <2 cells or ss_within = 0.
  * ``total_var`` = ``VAR_SAMP(per_cell_value)`` -- gene-level denominator.
  * ``group_means_json`` = JSON dict {group: mean}, so the endpoint can
    hydrate its response without a DuckDB round-trip.

Facet handling:

  * Facets are auto-discovered from the dataset's ``.md`` obs block:
    every column starting with ``ant_``.
  * ``ant_braak`` (numerical) is treated as categorical here (each
    level is its own group). For truly continuous facets, we NTILE(5)
    into ``q1``..``q5`` and treat those as categories.
  * Skips facets with 1 unique value (no groups) or n_unique > 50 (per
    spec: uninformative for group-variance).
  * Skips ``cell_name``.

Scope:

  * Restricted to the genes already present in
    ``<h5adstore>/gene_stats_index.parquet`` (the "hot set"). This is
    task #324's promise; the full-genome sweep is task #330.

Usage:
  ant-gene-variance-precompute [--only DB1,DB2,...] [--out PATH]
                               [--workers N] [--force] [--dry-run]
                               [--h5adstore-root DIR]
                               [--max-facet-cardinality N]
                               [--gene-index PATH]
"""
